```java
public class Cart {
    public java.util.List<String> items = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
}

cart.items.clear(); // external code wipes internal state directly — no control
```

```java
public class Cart {
    private final java.util.List<String> items = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
    public void add(String item) { items.add(item); }   // controlled mutation
    public java.util.List<String> getItems() {
        return java.util.List.copyOf(items);            // defensive, unmodifiable copy
    }
}
```
Callers get behavior, not direct access — and the getter hands back a copy they can't mutate.
